        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Austria, Vienna, Graz, Spielfeld, Slovenia, Semmering, Bruck an der Mur, Gloggnitz, Mürzzuschlag\n- Systems: Southern Railway, Semmering railway, Wien Liesing railway station\n\nFacts:\n- Wien Liesing railway station opened in 1841 together with the Southern Railway.\n- The Southern Railway in Austria runs from Vienna to Graz and to the border with Slovenia at Spielfeld via Semmering and Bruck an der Mur.\n- The Semmering railway in Austria starts at Gloggnitz and leads over the Semmering to Mürzzuschlag.\n- The Semmering railway was the first mountain railway in Europe built with a standard-gauge track.",
